Skill: GitHub `gh` + `git` on the **remote runner** for issue/PR comments and auth bootstrap. **Commit, push, and draft PR** are owned by `stage-runner.sh commit-pr` (spawn-context Commit-pr) — not hand-written `gh pr create` in subagent goals.

Keywords: github, gh cli, git, pull request, pr comment, issue comment, branch, commit, push, cdk, typescript, python.

========================================================================
1) Tool boundary
========================================================================

- Shell runner tools only: `${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_command`, `${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_series`.
- Clone once via `clone-pack.sh` — never per-file `gh api /repos/.../contents/`.
- PR open/update: ONE `create-pr-runner` → `stage-runner.sh commit-pr` (orchestration Template D+F).

========================================================================
2) Auth bootstrap (once per subagent series)
========================================================================

From runner env (`typed_secret_refs.github`):

  GIT_TOKEN from GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN → export GH_TOKEN
  gh auth setup-git
  git config user.name / user.email (stackgen-cdk-bot)

If token missing: stop with clone/auth blocker — never `gh auth token` or notes with raw tokens.

========================================================================
3) Issue / PR comments (Template E — create-pr-comment / create-pr-notify)
========================================================================

Inputs from notes: `repository_full_name`, `issue_or_pr_number`, `pr_url`, `validation_summary`, `test_summary_tail`, `module_quality_summary`, `stage_summary:*`, `gate_result`.

- `pr_url` set → `gh pr comment` with validation summary + test excerpt.
- Else → `gh issue comment` or `gh api .../issues/.../comments`.
- Blocked stages: include "## Workflow blocked" quoting `stage_summary:*=blocked`.

========================================================================
4) Read / edit CDK sources (from local clone only)
========================================================================

After `repo_clone_path=$WORK_ROOT/repo`:

- TypeScript CDK: `lib/`, `bin/`, `test/`, `package.json`, `cdk.json`
- Python CDK: `app.py`, `tests/`, `requirements.txt`, `cdk.json`
- Discovery catalog repos (legacy): provider/module dirs — see `${sop_discovery_modules_layout}` when enabled

Use `rg`, `cat`, `sed` in execute_series — not GitHub Contents API.

========================================================================
5) Failure modes
========================================================================

- `gh auth` fails → auth blocker; validate stage may post Template E notify only.
- `git push` non-fast-forward → fetch/rebase on `working_branch`, re-run validate, push again.
- PR already exists → commit-pr pushes to same branch (rework loop).
